    "api_error_status": null,
    "result": "I wrote `AddMember`, but I could not compile or test it. The sandbox asks for approval on every `go` command, so neither `members_test.go` nor the Linux build has run.\n\nHow it behaves:\n- **Retries:** if the name is already in the list, it returns nil and does not touch the file. This means one name can join only once. If two different people can share a name, the API needs a request ID to tell them apart.\n- **Concurrent calls:** a mutex handles calls in the same process. An OS lock on `path.lock` handles other processes. The OS drops that lock when the process dies, so a crash cannot leave a stale lock.\n- **Crash during a write:** it writes to `path.tmp`, syncs it to disk, then renames it over `path`, so a crash leaves either the old file or the new one. A `.tmp` file left by a crash gets overwritten on the next run.\n- **Empty file:** treated as no members, like a missing file.\n\nNew files: `lock_unix.go` and `lock_windows.go` (the OS lock for each platform) and `members_test.go`. The tests cover repeated calls, 50 names each sent 3 times at once, and a leftover `.tmp` file.\n\nTo check it, run `go test -race ./...`.",
